From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:46:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(approval): do not ask about reads or the operator's own
 clones

Smart approval asked Jacob about ls, grep and git log inside a clone of his own private repo, and about subagent tests. Three causes: a process://claude-pool judge (Claude Code calling hosted Sonnet) counted as self-hosted because its unqualified host name looks local, so its allow on a session fetch was downgraded to a question; read-only commands were still routed through the session-fetch hold when the pre-filter missed them (2>/dev/null, git -C <dir>); and every clone of any source was treated as external code.

Only an http(s) endpoint can now be a self-hosted judge; process:// and other pseudo-addresses count as hosted. A command made only of reading programs never carries the session-fetch fact, including with redirects to /dev/null and git -C or --no-pager. New approvals.trusted_sources lists URL prefixes (git@github.com:me/, https://github.com/me/); a path cloned from one is not external code. There is no default; a look-alike, a ".." path, or a clone with -c, -u or --upload-pack is not trusted; a dangerous command pattern still skips stage 1.

A stage-1 reply with no verdict is retried once with a stricter format line on the user turn (the rules are unchanged), then stage 2 runs; a stage-1 window error or failure runs stage 2 before the user is asked; a stage-2 reply with no verdict is retried once. Also folds in the review prompt fix: runs_in_session_fetch stays out of the action text and only routes the review.
